      {
        "id": 10989,
        "name": "LeperKhan",
        "username": "LeperKhan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/leperkhan/{size}/1894_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-16T07:19:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Man, this board has come alive with questions! I'm sure more are to come up as we go along, but one came up today that I wasn't sure how to 'resolve.'&nbsp;</p><p>On Synaptic Interruption, after blocking the attack and sending those blocked attacks back to your attacker, does the attacker then get a chance to roll defenses against what is essentially their own attack? We had been playing that those are freebie hits on the attacker, but that seems overly powerful from an already powerful character.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:11.751Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 10989,
        "topic_slug": "tachyon-card-help",
        "display_username": "LeperKhan",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Man, this board has come alive with questions! I&#39;m sure more are to come up as we go along, but one came up today that I wasn&#39;t sure how to &#39;resolve.&#39;&nbsp;</p><p>On Synaptic Interruption, after blocking the attack and sending those blocked attacks back to your attacker, does the attacker then get a chance to roll defenses against what is essentially their own attack? We had been playing that those are freebie hits on the attacker, but that seems overly powerful from an already powerful character.</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 8247,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 2,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 115010,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-16T07:51:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, you always defend against an attack. You reassign the dice that you blocked as an attack from tachyon, so you pretend like Tachyon was attacking them and happened to roll the same numbers on the dice.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:03.876Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 10989,
        "topic_slug": "tachyon-card-help",
        "display_username": "McBehrer",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
