      {
        "id": 115012,
        "name": "LeperKhan",
        "username": "LeperKhan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/leperkhan/{size}/1894_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-16T16:48:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One important thing to note on \"re-assigned\" attacks is that you cannot add dice to it with attack+1 tokens, nor will it trigger using an attack-1 token. &nbsp;You also can't use aim to affect it. &nbsp;Those exact dice will be reassigned, you can't affect them otherwise.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There's no doubt in my mind that you are correct, as you are a Playtester and I'm sure needed to have these discussions, so is this spelled out somewhere in the rule book? I'm glad this whole community is here to clarify things, but it's a shame the rulebook is so lacking in specifications for many situations. I'm sure that when the \"Cards\" section of the website is updated, things will be clearer, but for now we are just kind of randomly deciding things at home, hahaha.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:04.019Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
